  "fact": {
    "heading": "📖 *The journal context of 1924*",
    "fact_type": "first_publication",
    "source_ids": [
      "esenin-tired-bibliography"
    ],
    "text": "Esenin wrote the poem in 1923, and its first publication followed in 1924 in the journal «Гостиница для путешествующих в прекрасном». It appeared beside texts connected with «Москва кабацкая», placing the speaker’s fatigue and memory of the Ryazan landscape within a broader group of poems rather than as a single isolated confession."
  },
  "question": {
    "lead": "_In this English adaptation:_",
    "text": "which contrast remains strongest — the remembered Ryazan sky, the city, or the speaker’s weariness?"
  },
